From 7576afbd2f39c63be997e95f080ef2b07a3a2a6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:54:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 82/88] route: log a connection without a fakeip record as a
 warning that says why

A connection to a FakeIP address the store has no record for is refused by design when
no sniffed domain rescues it (a protocol that names no domain: SSH, a UDP game), but the
refusal was logged at the error level as a bare "missing fakeip record", once per
connection and per new UDP session of a flow, for as long as the client held the address.

It is now a warning with the address and the reasons a record can be missing, in the
three places that log routing errors. The error itself is unchanged: the connection is
refused as before.
---
 route/route.go          |  17 +++++-
 route/route_log_test.go | 131 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 145 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 route/route_log_test.go

